  "# Codegen co-scientist, iteration 26

Iteration 25 asked to remove `back-edge?` only against a wider amu
execution run, or keep it and measure call + back-edge across a spill.
This file takes the spill measurement. WIP=1 was this hole, not
predicate removal.

Do not overwrite 04-25.

## What ran

amu's `pressure-loop-module` is the iteration-25 count-loop plus five
loop-invariant constants whose textual last-use is after the latch, so
the interval covers the back-edge. Sum is 31; return is n+31. Under
the scratch tier those five plus n/acc do not fit, so the scanner must
spill.

Probe encodings:

- production: `:all-vregs` 18 slots
- override full-pool aarch64: `:call-live` 0 spills (preserved absorbs)
- override full-pool x86: `:call-live` 4 stores
- override scratch-only both ISAs: `:call-live` 8 stores / 10 loads

`a-call-and-a-back-edge-across-a-spill-execute` (scratch-only +
`back-edge?` false):

- policy `:call-live` on both targets; spill-store and spill-load
  counts `pos?` so it is a spill
- kexe n∈{0,1,5,50} equals n+31, no `KEXE_TRAP`, both ISAs
- `(pos? @calls)` so green is not an unapplied redef
- production (no override): same oracle, `:all-vregs`

Judah: `isa-execution-test` **19 tests, 729 assertions, 0 failures**
(was 18/688). Available ISAs: `[aarch64 x86_64]`. Slot count is not
the claim.

## What this is not

Not predicate removal. A spill executing on the scanner path is
encodings plus kexe for this fixture, not a license to drop
`back-edge?` for the suite. Production still all-vreg via the guard.

Not cfg-liveness. Allocator code is unchanged (`ac14016d` / `69e364e`).
deps.edn was not bumped. kotoba-mir and kotoba-native were not moved.

